{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json,ast,hashlib,subprocess\nr=json.loads(subprocess.check_output(['python3','tools.py','resolve','run://r-001'],text=True))\nc=r['context']; hist={t['id']:t for t in c['history']}\nprotocol=r['required_study_protocol_ref']\nbase=ast.parse(Path('candidate.py').read_text())\nconfig=ast.literal_eval(next(n.value for n in base.body if isinstance(n,ast.Assign) and any(isinstance(t,ast.Name) and t.id=='CONFIG' for t in n.targets)))\nnames=[('state_adaptive_none','candidate.py','candidate','state_adaptive','none'),('state_uniform_none','state_uniform_none.py','control','state_uniform','none'),('state_adaptive_prior','state_adaptive_prior.py','candidate','state_adaptive','adaptive'),('state_uniform_prior','state_uniform_prior.py','control','state_uniform','adaptive')]\nfixed=['Protocol '+protocol+'; same feature/label identities, visibility, official split and all training examples', 'One pass, batch 8192, history 100; host train_seed 20262027 for this contrast, unchanged split dense AdamW / embedding Adagrad, learning rates, clipping and BF16/TF32 policy', 'All g0 representation paths, masks, counts, rank moments, feedback memory, JointBlock, task towers and sum-four-BCE objective', 'Identical inherited constructor order, parameter tensors, task identities, two refinement stages, terminal low-rank value reconstruction, zero-initialized residual output', 'Same sanitized historical events and target fields; no current action, timestamps, labels or new inputs in forward']\ncontrasts=[{\n 'parent_ref':'g1-r0006-hybrid_none',\n 'intervention':'state_adaptive_none: replace only the memory addressed by the two narrow refinement reads: intact final g0 field/relation tokens instead of projected raw events. Final wide pooling still uses raw event keys/values and no match prior.',\n 'control':'Reuse g1-r0006-hybrid_none as the exact event-memory source comparator (macro AUC 0.8304505973621781), with source hash 2f89f26d5716aa0aa4e3cf3dc805a850e26bc57a45472ed4e863df594a2f6374. Also compare frozen entry g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate and initial baseline-din. query_memory=events retains exact source operations for a host parity check; it is not an additional uncounted training arm.',\n 'held_fixed':fixed,\n 'remaining_confounds':['Memory substitution intentionally changes semantic units and key length; measured compute can differ. New structured reads use explicit FP32 softmax while historical narrow reads use SDPA, so the historical comparison alone cannot distinguish numerical-kernel effects.', 'One existing seed is exploratory; same-seed rerunning the old control is not a new independent mechanism contrast. Source labels and offline history semantics limit interpretation.', 'Task-dependent gradients through g0 tokens change optimization. Equal parameter count alone does not identify the causal route.'],\n 'decision_if_supported':'Require gain over BOTH source bests, the current hybrid_none incumbent, and the concurrent uniform state control, with all per-task changes and measured costs. Advance only as preliminary support for this local information-flow adaptation; repeat paired seeds and retain a capacity/optimization explanation until controls disagree.',\n 'decision_if_not_supported':'If no gain over current incumbent or gain costs more without better quality, retain the existing model on the measured frontier. If uniform also gains, attribute only to structured-memory substitution/transform, not query-conditioned addressing. Preserve the failed branch; do not infer general incompatibility from one implementation.'\n},{\n 'parent_ref':'g1-r0006-hybrid_none',\n 'intervention':'Compare state_adaptive_none to state_uniform_none: learned per-head, per-task Q/K softmax over valid g0 state tokens versus equal weights over exactly the same valid tokens at each of two refinement reads.',\n 'control':'state_uniform_none is an active content/transform control: same memory tokens, LayerNorm/Q/K/V/output modules, state mixers, explicit FP32 score and weight calculations, terminal Q/K and low-rank readout. It supplies the masked mean of normalized/projected state rather than removing the branch.',\n 'held_fixed':fixed+['No terminal match prior; identical memory tensor and valid-token masks; identical new source except literal query_memory CONFIG'],\n 'remaining_confounds':['Uniform routing intentionally has a restricted functional space, although nominal parameters are identical. The same Q/K remain trainable through final pooling and task mixers; effective gradients and backward cost need not match.', 'The query learns jointly with g0 representations, so the contrast supports the utility of conditional addressing under this recipe rather than a unique explanation for every gain.'],\n 'decision_if_supported':'Consistent learned-over-uniform gain, also exceeding the current incumbent and surviving paired repetition, supports conditional use of g0 structured state beyond an extra normalized mean transform. Do not claim a novel attention mechanism.',\n 'decision_if_not_supported':'If uniform ties or wins, reject the conditional-addressing explanation for this implementation; any historical gain remains attributable to memory substitution, scaling or optimization. Prefer the cheaper supported arm and retain null outcomes.'\n},{\n 'parent_ref':'g1-r0006-hybrid_adaptive',\n 'intervention':'2x2 factorial: state_adaptive_prior - state_adaptive_none versus state_uniform_prior - state_uniform_none. Terminal prior is the inherited bounded [0,2] adaptive five-identity-field match bias; no new prior form or strength is tuned.',\n 'control':'All four concurrent arms have identical parameters, constructors and structured-memory computations. Cross prior on/off within each routing mode. Use existing g1-r0006-hybrid_adaptive versus g1-r0006-hybrid_none as the historical event-memory interaction comparison, not a randomized repeated estimate.',\n 'held_fixed':fixed+['Both prior modes calculate adaptive/uniform/rotated prior tensors with the inherited implementation; only the selected additive bias changes', 'Same five match channels, padding-ID exclusions and current-target unknown-action protection'],\n 'remaining_confounds':['Source prior routing results are small, single-seed differences without cluster-bootstrap intervals. New factorial alone cannot establish that a prior is useful in all representations.', 'Prior and query weights share Q/K; any interaction can be optimization-mediated. The concurrent uniform read controls query dependence, not all possible capacity-matched architectures.'],\n 'decision_if_supported':'Compute interaction (A_prior-A_none)-(U_prior-U_none), report both simple effects and per-task effects. A positive interaction AND positive prior effect in learned routing, persisting across paired seeds and overall improvement beyond source bests/incumbent, would support restored prior utility; otherwise limit conclusions to whichever component has controlled support.',\n 'decision_if_not_supported':'If prior is neutral/harmful again, retain the no-prior branch if its own addressing contrast succeeds. Do not rescue the prior by changing its strength post hoc in this study. Uniform_prior gains alone do not support adaptive addressing.'\n}]\nstudy={\n 'id':'g1-t001-structured-query-memory-followup',\n 'protocol_ref':protocol,\n 'evidence_refs':c['allowed_observation_ids'],\n 'question':'Can g1-style evolving task queries use the committed g0 structured state more effectively than repeated raw-event refinement, improving validation four-task macro ROC-AUC beyond both frozen source bests and the current hybrid_none incumbent at justified measured cost? Does retaining structure restore terminal match-prior utility?',\n 'hypothesis':'Observed limitation: g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate scored 0.8301982212762624; g1-r0004-match_terminal_only scored 0.8192325306335276. The first hybrid factorial scored adaptive=0.8301475468560667, none=0.8304505973621781, uniform=0.8301706875648142, rotated=0.8299633162511856. Thus neither adaptive nor rotation contrasts support extra match-prior utility on g0. hybrid_none is the current validation incumbent, not proof of a mechanism. Inspection shows g0 already supplies six target-match relation summaries with rank moments plus joint feedback memory; the hybrid compresses their final state to a common mean and then makes two raw-event reads. Provisional mechanism: these redundant raw-event refinement reads fail to exploit distinctions among g0 fields/relations. Replacing their memory with the intact final g0 tokens lets evolving task queries condition terminal event retrieval on structured evidence without more parameters. If match bias was redundant rather than poorly conditioned, it should remain unhelpful even after this replacement. Mean information loss, prior redundancy and task interference remain alternatives, not established facts.',\n 'nearest_work':[\n  {'source_ref':'trial://g1-r0006-hybrid_none','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Verified exact starting candidate/source hash. Keep all modules, initialization, mean seed, two stages and final event pooling. Replace the memory for the two narrow reads by g0 final tokens; add a uniform-addressing control, no parameter increase.'},\n  {'source_ref':'trial://g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Verified pinned source hash and inspected inherited representation: target-weighted global/rank-bin/field-match summaries, position/content maps and separate joint feedback memory. Add only the inherited four-task residual retrieval branch, now reading this structured state before terminal raw-event pooling.'},\n  {'source_ref':'trial://g1-r0004-match_terminal_only','verification':'implementation_checked','difference':'Inspected full source: evolving field+task stream reads raw events, with same-field prior at terminal pooling and low-rank values. Here preserve g0 state/towers, keep only four query tokens, use g0 state as refinement memory, and cross the unchanged terminal prior rather than assuming its source gain transfers.'},\n  {'source_ref':'unirank-code:INFNet','verification':'read','difference':'Read pinned primary benchmark implementation lines 204-313, git 90bb99a60724e975ec565836266fd86dcad0039d, text hash e3750a73af1ceb6b2be4bf9355b70a9ad356985a3c465ef27238ef7e0f28fb4c. Hubs aggregate categorical/sequence/task groups and broadcast affine gated updates. This adaptation keeps one-way masked reads, no hub broadcasts or sequence updates, and reuses g0 relation tokens. Benchmark aggregation documents mask-free attention; it is not copied. Original INFNet paper is provenance-only and not audited; no equivalence/priority claim.'},\n  {'source_ref':'paper:din','verification':'read','difference':'Read archived primary text lines 29-103, arXiv 1706.06978v4, content hash 5fee25f33f375e51b3ee9417d376ff9dbe2ea3628c932a7679ddfeb0feaaade2. Inherit adapted target-conditioned local-activation sums/Dice through g0, but use relation-token interactions and four evolving query states rather than one shared sum alone. No exact original-DIN reproduction or novel-attention claim.'},\n  {'source_ref':'paper:dmr','verification':'read','difference':'Only pinned author README is available and read (9 lines, hash 656c9e5eec79c9843e907a555ede2bf0a66a0db3515916af3d655080057c5a75); publisher text unavailable. Its category/brand/behavior input warning does not replace this frozen benchmark\\\\'s actual previous-exposure item IDs. No claim about full DMR architecture or new superiority.'}\n ],\n 'inherited_components':[\n  'All g0 six-item-field/action embeddings, static fields, signed DIN local activation, five temporal bins x seven relation summary tokens, full linear position moments, relation/content banks, factorized feedback-content maps and separate joint feedback memory',\n  'g0 strict history/ID sanitization, zero/padding exclusion for equality evidence, action masking, field/relation identities, JointBlock, raw static and global-value skip, four task towers',\n  'g1-r0006-hybrid_none event projection, rank position embeddings, task identities, shared pre-normalized TaskRead Q/K/V, two TaskMixers, terminal head-averaged raw-value pooling, rank-32 value reconstruction/nonaffine normalization and zero-start residual output',\n  'Unmodified terminal match-prior adaptive/none routes, unchanged field channels, fixed gain 2, no added labels/losses or frozen training changes'\n ],\n 'proposed_difference':'At each of the two existing task-query refinement stages, replace read(states, projected_raw_events, history_valid) with read_state(states, final_g0_tokens, token_valid). Final wide read remains over the same projected raw events and original values. read_state reuses existing Q/K/V/output and computes strictly masked FP32 softmax; learned and uniform valid-token routes are crossed with terminal_prior adaptive/none (four standalone modules). The events compatibility mode retains exact historical operations for host parity, without a fifth proposed training arm. No new modules/parameters, no query depth change, no altered representation or towers. This is a local adaptation of existing mechanisms; novelty remains unclaimed.',\n 'predictions':[\n  'Primary: state_adaptive_none should beat both g0 0.8301982212762624 and g1 source 0.8192325306335276 AND the stronger current hybrid_none incumbent 0.8304505973621781. Merely beating the weaker source or an imported number at higher cost is not success.',\n  'Conditional-addressing prediction: state_adaptive_none > state_uniform_none and, separately, state_adaptive_prior > state_uniform_prior. Uniform controls retain active state content and transformations, so ties oppose the query-specific addressing explanation.',\n  'Prior compatibility prediction is discriminating, not assumed: if improved query conditioning restores useful matches, adaptive prior will have positive simple effect under learned state reads and a positive 2x2 interaction. If prior is redundant with g0 relations, prior effects will stay null/negative even if state reads improve.',\n  'Exploratory slices retain the existing predeclared history bins (empty,1-16,17-64,>64) and all per-task sample/positive/negative counts. Addressing gains are expected primarily on nonempty long histories; empty-history residual updates must be exactly zero. Do not promote noisy rare-task empty-slice gains to mechanism evidence.',\n  'Parameter count should remain exactly 33070309 total, 31793216 embeddings, 1277093 dense, conditional on the same feature map; only 47904 more dense parameters than g0. New narrow reads address static_count+35 rather than L=100 keys, but explicit FP32 versus SDPA and gradient differences prevent asserting lower runtime before measurement.'\n ],\n 'falsifiers':[\n  'Failure to exceed the stronger source and current incumbent on equal-weight validation macro AUC falsifies added predictive utility for this implementation. Gains entirely reproduced by uniform reads oppose conditional addressing; an isolated winning seed does not establish compatibility.',\n  'Nonpositive prior simple effect and interaction oppose restored prior utility. Even if learned state reads win, report a negative prior finding rather than claiming g0/g1 match-mechanism complementarity.',\n  'A gain that disappears on paired repetition, relies on one rare/noisy task slice, or is dominated on measured training/inference cost weakens or defeats the intended claim. Report AUC and Logloss of every task with deltas to baseline, g0 and current incumbent, without adding a per-task veto.',\n  'Any future-label/current-action dependence, invalid-padding sensitivity, nonfinite values/gradients, parameter mismatch or inherited-initialization parity failure invalidates the implementation. Stop and retain charged failures; do not change protocol to pass.'\n ],\n 'alternative_explanations':[\n  'Single-seed optimization variation and validation selection optimism; source bests are frozen selected trials, not independent replications.',\n  'Exact-match prior duplicates g0 relation evidence; mismatched task utilities can offset macro gains. hybrid_none versus g0 AUC deltas were click -0.0002928621, cart +0.0007996453, fav +0.0020600729, buy -0.0015573517; corresponding Logloss deltas were -0.0000538249,-0.0000695311,-0.0000362881,+0.0000317096. Cart/fav gains are accompanied by buy/click losses.',\n  'The full structured state changes gradient routing, scale/normalization and memory distribution, not solely information content. Learned-versus-uniform controls share numerical implementation, while historical raw-event comparison retains a kernel confound.',\n  'Additional active retrieval capacity and transformed normalized means can explain gains over g0. Uniform state reads and existing no-prior raw-event branch are needed before attributing a benefit to query-conditioned structured-state access.',\n  'Input auxiliary outcomes match category/brand over 24h rather than ad-specific attribution; official_offline action maturity and whole-window vocabulary assumptions limit production or causal interpretation. DMR\\\\'s different input semantics must not be imported.',\n  'Initial observations show no supported adaptive-versus-uniform advantage in the previous hybrid (adaptive -0.0000231407 versus uniform); the worse rotation alone is insufficient. No failed execution is present in authorized history, and no unseen earlier lineage result is imported as local evidence.'\n ],\n 'contrasts':contrasts,\n 'cost_plan':{\n  'estimate_ref':'Authorized measured receipts: baseline-din wall/train=329.11/293.07s; g0-r0011-memory_joint_separate=490.25/443.35s; g1-r0004-match_terminal_only=853.70/811.08s; all four g1-r0006 hybrids=1005.54..1009.71s wall, 952.87..956.32s train, ~43.24..44.02s inference. g0 inference=37.64s, median model batch latency=48.81ms; hybrid_none=43.35s and65.13ms. Use ~1010s per new complete unit, not stale protocol 483.42s calibration. Frozen per-trial hard cap=1208.5413760878146s; 4-arm ceiling=4834.17s, planning estimate4040s. Remaining runtime snapshot=15317.398981809616s before this preparation; all preparation consumes it. No raw data/GPU/torch is exposed here; host owns data digest verification, numerical preflight, training and scoring.',\n  'all_variants_counted':True,\n  'attribution_reserve':'Reserve 6000s for host numerical checks, any charged failures and paired repetitions. When feasible, target three host-authorized paired seeds of selected learned arm and its same-prior uniform control: four additional complete units <=4834.17s plus <=1165.83s diagnostics. Do not set new seeds or frozen optimizer parameters in candidate CONFIG. Keep the existing raw-event and g0 comparisons; repeat g0/current raw incumbent only if remaining budget also preserves assessment reserve. A source-comparison gain without source repetitions remains preliminary.',\n  'assessment_reserve':'Reserve 3000s for a frozen validation-only comparison suite, report/uncertainty and host validation assessment. Freeze selected source/config/checkpoint hashes, g0 and g1 source bests, current hybrid_none, the chosen same-prior uniform control and key prior factorial arms, paired repetition seeds and authorized commands before assessment. No test interface exists; no held-out request, scores or predictions are authorized. Paired user-cluster bootstrap only if host exposes authorized validation user groups/predictions; do not reconstruct unavailable user IDs or invent intervals.',\n  'stop_rule':'Never exceed the frozen campaign deadline or1208.5413760878146s per-trial cap. Launch a complete unit only if its conservative cap, required diagnostics and remaining attribution/assessment reserves fit the live host ledger; no uncounted calibration, screening, retry or compatibility training. Initial planning commitment4834.17+6000+3000=13834.17s leaves1483.23s from the runtime snapshot for preparation/slack; debit elapsed preparation first and reduce scope if necessary. If four arms cease to fit, keep the no-prior learned/uniform pair first and explicitly omit prior interaction conclusions rather than silently dropping a control. If no useful complete controlled unit fits, stop. A timeout is an execution/cost failure, not scientific counterevidence. Exhausting resources is not success.'\n }\n}\nvariants=[]\nfor name,file,role,memory,prior in names:\n cfg=dict(config,query_memory=memory,terminal_prior=prior)\n digest=hashlib.sha256(Path(file).read_bytes()).hexdigest()\n variants.append({'name':name,'file':file,'role':role,'config':cfg,'note':f'Prospective untrained standalone module; source SHA256 {digest}. Same inherited parameters and initialization in all arms; only query_memory/terminal_prior differ. No local numerical result claimed. Host must verify finite BF16 forward/sum-four-BCE/backward, same-seed state_dict parameter equality, query_memory=events source forward/gradient parity with g1-r0006-hybrid_none or hybrid_adaptive, zero-start g0 prediction parity, strict padding and current-action invariance, null/zero/singleton/full/mixed history handling, token masks and uniform routing before training. After a host update or controlled nonzero output perturbation verify active branch gradients and sensitivity again because zero output blocks upstream branch gradients at initialization. Check output probabilities [B,1] for all four labels. Measure parameter/train/inference/peak-memory costs, report all four AUC/Logloss deltas; effective backward cost may differ. No training/installations in coding workspace.'})\nassessments=[\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-infnet','decision':'used','rationale':'Pinned benchmark aggregation/broadcast source inspected as nearest work. Its task-aware multi-view aggregation motivates the controlled read of retained g0 structured state; this is external design provenance, not local effectiveness evidence. Previous declared use produced no supported match-prior gain; revise that explanation rather than erase the null result. Original paper detail remains unaudited.', 'transformed_mechanism':'Reuse existing four task queries and tied Q/K/V to read final g0 field/relation tokens at both query-refinement stages; retain one-way exact masks, no global-to-local broadcast, unchanged raw-event terminal pool. Uniform active addressing controls the proposed query dependence.', 'variant_names':[x[0] for x in names], 'nearest_work_difference':'No new hubs, separate group fusion or affine gated broadcasts. Parameter-neutral memory substitution within the imported hybrid, with an explicit routing-by-prior factorial and strictly masked state keys.', 'falsifier':'No gain beyond current hybrid_none and source bests, gains matched by uniform addressing, or cost/seed effects explaining the gain oppose this tested utility claim.'},\n {'knowledge_id':'unirank-method-ultrahstu','decision':'considered','rationale':'Retrieved card documents hybrid sparse/full sequence transduction; no original-paper audit or local support is available. Full sequence updates are not needed for the observed mean-seed/refinement limitation and would confound this bounded memory substitution.', 'transformed_mechanism':'None; no HSTU transduction, sparsity pattern or active-sequence truncation adopted.', 'variant_names':[], 'nearest_work_difference':'Fixed100-event visibility; read-only g0 token memory for four queries, original events only for final pooling. No comparative claim against UltraHSTU.', 'falsifier':'A later primary audit and matched-cost experiment showing useful event-state updates would reopen this option; this study cannot refute that architecture.'}\n]\nproposal={'study':study,'parent_trial':'g1-r0006-hybrid_none','variants':variants,'knowledge_assessments':assessments}\nPath('proposal.json').write_text(json.dumps(proposal,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nprint('Wrote proposal.json with',len(variants),'variants and',len(contrasts),'predeclared contrasts.')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
